@short_brief
# prose-audit: Grade A — The one-page alternative states who the alliance is, what each partner brought, what we can and cannot do from opposition, and the spring 2020 test, without requiring the nine-page chain.
title: The short version
subtitle: Who we are, what we hold, and what is coming
face-image: img/poland/events/wlodzimierz-czarzasty-2019.webp
new-page: true

= The short version

**We are Lewica** — not a party, an alliance of five things that needed each
other in July and now have to share a corridor for four years. SLD brings the
machine: the legal committee, the account, the regional structures and thirty
years of habits. Wiosna brings the face: Robert Biedroń, a secular and
progressive politics with no memory of 2004 attached to it. Razem brings the
programme and the organisers, refuses to merge into anyone, and takes its
decisions by member vote. Around them stand the trade unionists, the feminists
who kept the abortion-rights movement alive while we had no deputies, and a
small PPS current older than every other party in this room.

We have just re-entered the Sejm, with 49 deputies out of 460 and two
senators, after four years in which the Polish left held no seat at all. That
is enough to be heard and nowhere near enough to legislate. PiS has the
majority, the Presidential Palace, the Constitutional Tribunal and the evening
news; from opposition we can delay, expose, defend and organise, and that is
the entire list.

Next spring there is a presidential election. Andrzej Duda runs for a second
term. Civic Coalition will run somebody and will spend the campaign telling us
that a left-wing candidate is a gift to PiS. We will run one anyway, because the
last time we tried, our candidate took 2.38%, and until that number is beaten
nobody treats this alliance as a serious force.

The majority opposite is beatable. It is not one party: Ziobro's people and
Gowin's people each hold enough deputies to end it whenever the price is right.
Our task between now and the autumn 2027 election is to be the reason the
country wants an alternative, and to still be one organisation when the chance
arrives.

The club meets in the morning.

